Run a local seat without virtual terminals on kernels that have none.

vt.c only issues the VT ioctls where the kernel has them (where their
header is included), but vt_get_unused() still handed out VT numbers
everywhere, so
every X server of the seat was started with "vt1 -novtswitch" -- an option
a server built without VT support rejects, and the seat never comes up.
Elsewhere the seat now runs its display servers without a VT:

  - vt_supported() says whether the kernel has VTs (VT_ACTIVATE known);
  - vt_get_unused() returns -1 without them, so X gets no vtN argument;
  - the seat does not offer multiple sessions (user switching would start
    a second display server on the one screen);
  - the active session is the one LightDM activated, as on seats that
    have no VTs by nature, instead of "none" from the VT lookup.

